An IAM user in an AWS Organizations member account cannot create an S3 bucket. Root and OU SCPs permit the action. The following is the only SCP attached directly to this account:

{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Action":["cloudtrail:*","iam:*"],"Resource":"*"}]}

The user has this identity policy:

{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Action":"s3:*","Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::*"},{"Effect":"Deny","NotAction":"s3:*","NotResource":"arn:aws:s3:::*"}]}

No other policy or control changes this evaluation. Why is s3:CreateBucket denied?
